  "invariants": [
    "Both engines use unchanged shared ListBinding, Lists and Inputs. The single GNUstep provider owns actual NSBrowser/NSMatrix/cells/scrollers. The adapter copies no control rendering, layout, selection, tracking or key algorithm.",
    "Blink original GetListItems recalculation, traversal, labels, visibility and DOMNodeIds supply the application model. Original option selectedness and select multiple mode supply list-specific state; stable DOM identities are re-resolved across native input and original callbacks.",
    "ThemePainter::Paint sends listbox appearance directly to CSS. The common theme/border wrappers handle owned listboxes and delegate every other appearance to original dispatch, preserving existing text virtual hooks. Guarded style data at +4, uint64 +56 bits 15..19 identifies appearance 5; compiled public struct stores and actual runtime confirm the enum.",
    "Original ListBoxSelectType::SaveLastSelection, HTMLOptionElement::setSelectedForBinding and ListBoxOnChange own DOM selectedness, dirty/validity/accessibility updates and trusted interaction completion. Only changed selectedness produces DOM input/change. Original trusted event dispatch, cancellation and focus remain intact.",
    "The original SetSelectedState method runs exactly once before owner invalidation for programmatic selection. Existing option-content/group-attribute observers also dirty the complete native owner. No synthetic script input/change events are introduced.",
    "Existing scroll-area scrollbar ownership suppresses duplicate engine bars for the measured native list; complete browser scroll/option geometry integration remains open. Loss of supported appearance and original frame detach release native ownership.",
    "The existing specific UA popup disabled rule is retained when appending list disabled/radius corrections. All corrections remain at UA origin below author/user styles. Broader styled controls are not qualified.",
    "The shared real-seat fixture compares whole native images and canonical DOM events. Independent native responder calls define key/focus results; a separate ordinary NSBrowser window replays outside gestures and records full cell visual state.",
    "Only the optional small Chromium adapter is rebuilt. Firefox adapter, browsers, AppKit/backend, shared provider/loader/shim and API 1/568 remain unchanged. Toolbars/address bars/tabs remain original. Future requested UI changes use optional app-specific patches over the same shared layer for subsequent GTK/Qt/KDE."
  ]
